@*
    Copy one Business Central environment into a new one - almost always a customer's
    production into a fresh sandbox, to try an update or reproduce a problem on real
    data. Shared by the environment page and the Environments list's row menu.

    The dialog only collects the answer - what the copy is called and what it is. The
    caller sends it (ProjectConnectionService.CopyEnvironmentAsync) and reports the
    outcome where its own page reports outcomes, so the two pages cannot word the same
    result differently. See .design/environment-updates.md, "Copying an environment".

    The confirm is re-voiced as the person chooses, which is why the dialog is opened on
    its own parameters rather than with per-call overrides: the button names the
    environment being made, and a production copy is a different, redder question from a
    sandbox one.
*@
@using ALDevToolbox.Services.ObjectExplorer.Bc

<ConfirmDialog @ref="_confirm"
               Wide="true"
               Title="@DialogTitle"
               Message="@DialogMessage"
               ConfirmLabel="@ConfirmLabel"
               ConfirmButtonClass="@ConfirmClass"
               ConfirmIcon="copy"
               ConfirmDisabled="@(NameProblem is not null)">
    <div class="field copy-env__name">
        <label class="field__label" for="copy-env-name">Name for the new environment</label>
        <input id="copy-env-name" class="input" type="text" required
               maxlength="@BcEnvironmentName.MaxLength" pattern="@BcEnvironmentName.Pattern"
               placeholder="e.g. CRONUS-Test" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
               aria-invalid="@(NameProblem is not null ? "true" : null)"
               aria-describedby="copy-env-name-help"
               value="@_name" @oninput="OnNameInput" />
        @* The rule as the person types, not after they submit: the name is the only
           thing they have to get right, and Business Central's refusal arrives minutes
           later as a code. An emptied field says so too - the button greys out either
           way, and a dead button with no reason beside it is a dead end. *@
        @if (NameProblem is { } problem)
        {
            <FieldError Id="copy-env-name-help" Message="@problem" />
        }
        else
        {
            <small id="copy-env-name-help" class="field__hint">@BcEnvironmentName.Rule</small>
        }
    </div>

    <fieldset class="copy-env__type">
        <legend class="copy-env__type-legend">What should the copy be?</legend>
        <label class="copy-env__type-opt">
            <input type="radio" name="copy-env-type"
                   checked="@(!IsProductionTarget)" @onchange="() => _type = BcEnvironmentTypes.Sandbox" />
            <span>Sandbox - for testing and training</span>
        </label>
        <label class="copy-env__type-opt">
            <input type="radio" name="copy-env-type"
                   checked="@IsProductionTarget" @onchange="() => _type = BcEnvironmentTypes.Production" />
            <span>Production - for the business to work in</span>
        </label>
    </fieldset>

    @* A note is drawn as an icon beside a body - the glyph carries the tone for anyone
       who cannot tell the tints apart, and without it the body sits in the icon's
       18px column and breaks a word to a line. *@
    <div class="copy-env__notes">
        @if (IsProductionTarget)
        {
            <p class="note note--danger">
                <span class="note__icon"><Icon Name="triangle-alert" Width="17" Height="17" /></span>
                <span class="note__body">
                    A production environment counts against @_customer's Business Central licences and
                    against the number of production environments they are allowed. Choose Sandbox
                    unless people are going to work in this one.
                </span>
            </p>
        }
        else if (_sourceIsProduction)
        {
            <p class="note note--warn">
                <span class="note__icon"><Icon Name="triangle-alert" Width="17" Height="17" /></span>
                <span class="note__body">
                    The sandbox will hold @_customer's real data - the same customers, invoices and
                    people as @_source. Everyone you let into it can read all of it.
                </span>
            </p>
        }
        @if (_storageFull)
        {
            <p class="note note--warn">
                <span class="note__icon"><Icon Name="database" Width="17" Height="17" /></span>
                <span class="note__body">
                    @_customer has already used up the storage their Business Central allows. A copy
                    takes as much room again as @_source, so Business Central may refuse it. Delete a
                    sandbox they no longer use, or ask them to buy more storage, first.
                </span>
            </p>
        }
    </div>

    @* Written for somebody who has not pressed the button yet: "you can close this"
       here means Cancel, and nothing has started. *@
    <p class="copy-env__wait">
        Business Central does the copying - an hour or more for a large environment. Once it has
        started you can leave the page; @_source's Operations tab shows how far it has got.
    </p>
</ConfirmDialog>

@code {
    /// <summary>What the person chose: what the copy is called, and what it is.</summary>
    public sealed record Copy(string Name, string Type);

    private ConfirmDialog? _confirm;
    private string _name = string.Empty;
    private string _type = BcEnvironmentTypes.Sandbox;
    private string _customer = string.Empty;
    private string _source = string.Empty;
    private bool _sourceIsProduction;
    private bool _storageFull;

    private bool IsProductionTarget => BcEnvironmentTypes.IsProduction(_type);

    /// <summary>Why the typed name won't do, or null. The same check the service makes.</summary>
    private string? NameProblem => BcEnvironmentName.Validate(_name);

    private string DialogTitle => $"Copy {_source}?";

    private string DialogMessage =>
        $"Business Central makes a new environment for {_customer} from {_source}, with everything it "
        + $"holds now - its data, its apps and its settings. {_source} itself is left alone.";

    /// <summary>The button says what it makes, so the name is read once more before the click.</summary>
    private string ConfirmLabel => NameProblem is null ? $"Copy to {_name.Trim()}" : "Copy";

    /// <summary>
    /// Red for a production copy, which is the choice that costs the customer a licence;
    /// the dialog takes its tint and its glyph from this.
    /// </summary>
    private string ConfirmClass => IsProductionTarget ? "btn--danger" : "btn--primary";

    /// <summary>
    /// Asks what the copy is called and what it is. Null when the person backed out.
    /// Sandbox is the default every time: a production copy is the rarer, dearer answer.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="tenantStorageUse">
    /// How full the customer's tenant is, as a fraction of its allowance (1 or more means
    /// at or over it). Null when we haven't read both halves; the dialog then says nothing
    /// about storage rather than guessing.
    /// </param>
    public async Task<Copy?> OpenAsync(
        string projectName, string sourceName, bool sourceIsProduction, double? tenantStorageUse = null)
    {
        if (_confirm is null) return null;
        _customer = projectName;
        _source = sourceName;
        _sourceIsProduction = sourceIsProduction;
        _storageFull = tenantStorageUse >= 1;
        _type = BcEnvironmentTypes.Sandbox;
        _name = BcEnvironmentName.Suggest(sourceName);
        StateHasChanged();

        var confirmed = await _confirm.OpenAsync();
        return confirmed && NameProblem is null ? new Copy(_name.Trim(), _type) : null;
    }

    /// <summary>The sentence for a page's success notice, so both callers say the same thing.</summary>
    public static string DoneMessage(Copy copy, string sourceName) =>
        // "Making X from Y", never "copying Y to X": the second reads as pushing one
        // environment's data into another that already exists, which is the one thing
        // this never does.
        $"Business Central is making {copy.Name} from {sourceName}. It takes a while; {copy.Name} "
        + "appears in the environments list once it is ready.";

    private void OnNameInput(ChangeEventArgs e) => _name = e.Value?.ToString() ?? string.Empty;
}
